# Code guidelines (validity harness)

- Prefer small, reviewable diffs; commit when a verifier-relevant unit is done.
- Do not mark work complete unless acceptance criteria, targeted tests, and QA
  evidence are present (completion boundary).
- Use repository MCP/tools before inventing APIs or component contracts.
- On failure, capture the failing check and repair within the iteration budget.
- Human PR review remains required; prepare a concise PR summary of risks.
